  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Desk Study - Bethlehem Biomass and Waste-to-Energy Project, through Niessen Consultants</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This desk study reviewed a proposal for a feasibility study to construct an advanced waste-to-energy facility for the Bethlehem Development Foundation (BDF) that would produce approximately fifteen megawatts of electricity. Recently, BDF has launched a comprehensive plan to modernize the existing Municipal Solid Waste (MSW) collection system with a new transfer station in Bethlehem and a permanent landfill site that will serve the two governorates of Bethlehem and Hebron.</narrative>
  </description>
